{
  "title": "make dev-headless server stuck in cargo watch restart loop",
  "description": "On 2026-10-07 in a fresh worktree (blurb-tablet), `make dev-headless` never brought the server up: the server log printed `[Running 'cargo run']` / `Compiling ramekin-server` 57 times in ~10 minutes, restarting roughly every 10s before the build finished. \
No tracked files under server/ or ramekin-core/ (excluding target/) had changed, so the trigger is unknown (possibly build outputs or a path cargo watch does not ignore). \
Workaround that worked: `SERVER_CMD=\"cargo run\" make dev-headless` (process-compose.yaml honors SERVER_CMD), which came up in ~6 minutes. \
Reproduce with a cold target/ dir, find what cargo watch is reacting to (e.g. `cargo watch -x run --why`), and add the right ignore or watch path so a cold start completes.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "dev-environment",
  ],
